<title>USA: Reebok says backlog rises 9.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Reebok says backlog rises 9.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOUGHTON, Mass. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reebok International Inc said on Thursday that its total backlog of open customer orders to be delivered from April 1997 through September 1997 for the Reebok brand was up 9.1 percent versus the same period one year ago.</p>
<p>The company said North American backlog was up 11.7 percent, and the international backlog was up 5 percent. On a constant dollar basis, the international backlog was up 9.1 percent.</p>
</text>
